From 9177dd2a72228d1f560d3800c2d033002a3fdd59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikhil Prakash <nikhil.prakash1995@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:20:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Test register: per-option, harness/stats, testbed Python,
 Phase 2, promote-step and layer-5 test bodies (TSR Phase 3)

Takes the parts of the staged TSR series that WM-2 A7 did not cover
(branch review 2026-10-24, T-12). build_register.py gains a static source
parser for test bodies with no per-test record: every it() under
test/L2-identity-system/per-option, test/benchmarks, phase2/idtx/test and
5_zkp-agent-identity/test-contracts, and every test function under
cv2x-testbed/tests, phase2/backends, tools/run_identity and
5_zkp-agent-identity/tests. Subject, function and class come from
docs/testing/unit_rules.yaml; each entry records the rule that mapped it;
no test title is edited. The 681 existing entries are unchanged; 529
entries added for 527 tests; per-directory Python counts equal pytest's
distinct collected functions. --check-complete fails on a tracked test
file that is neither registered, results-derived (A7's py_layers.json
covers 2_w3c-ssi-layer and sandbox/py-suites) nor excluded with a reason,
and on a parse/token count mismatch; both probes shown to fail.
